  "sourceUse": "The 2026–2027 TiSEM regulations, programme appendix pp. 59–60, and dated 3A200-2026 catalogue agree on the three years. The first two each contain 12 compulsory units. The third contains 30 EC of genuine choice, 18 EC of compulsory courses and a 12 EC thesis. GROW is strongly recommended, zero-credit extracurricular activity. Competence Compass is a distinct compulsory 3 EC unit.",
  "progression": {
    "yearOne": "Accounting, strategy, mathematics, marketing, organisational behaviour and applied business practice in autumn precede investment, economics, human resources, programming, operations and data analysis in spring. The OER sets the ordinary positive binding study advice threshold at 42 first-year EC.",
    "yearTwo": "The year builds on first-year courses through supply chains, strategic management, management accounting and data analysis, then consumer behaviour, information systems, corporate finance, research methods, law and a company project. The introductory data course explicitly prepares students for Data Analysis, research methods and the thesis.",
    "yearThree": "The autumn choice allows exchange, an internship plus an elective, two 15 EC school minor blocks or one 30 EC Tilburg minor. Art. 4.5 sets a 90 EC internship threshold and refers to the applicable handbook. The ordinary sequence can reach 120 EC before autumn. The older examples and dates embedded in the course entry are not applied to this cohort. The spring semester comprises three 6 EC courses and a 12 EC thesis. Art. 4.5 requires 120 EC for a sixth-semester thesis and 138 EC from semester seven, together with syllabus requirements. The catalogue describes an independent research project and defence. The normal sequence can reach 150 EC before the thesis semester."
  }
}
